prompt: Load the `kdevkit` skill from ~/.claude/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md or ~/.kiro/steering/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md — whichever path exists. Begin your response with the literal line `[kdevkit] applies` on its own line. Then answer in 4–8 sentences: the PR is approved and I say "ship it". What will you do to close the feature?
expect_substr: [kdevkit] applies
expected_narrative: A correct answer covers, in order: (1) reconcile in-flight markers in the feature spec — unchecked Implementation Plan items, open Decision Log entries, unresolved questions — either resolved in place or moved to backlog/follow-up; (2) squash merge to main as the default; mention the main-uses-merge-commits and FF-only-on-main exceptions; (3) branch cleanup local + remote without per-step prompts (deletion is the declared default); (4) soft project.md verify — re-run the §6 offer to update project.md, decline is fine; (5) interactive backlog cleanup — list backlog/ contents, ask user which items this feature resolves, git rm the chosen ones; (6) worktree teardown offer-only if the working dir is a non-primary worktree (do not auto-remove). Wrong answers: doing any of these without the explicit human cue; auto-removing the worktree; treating project.md update as a hard block; trying to detect resolved backlog items via metadata instead of asking; merging via plain merge by default; leaving the remote branch undeleted.
tools: claude,kiro
